        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: DOUGLAS R. COLE, ESQ., State Solicitor, Columbus, Ohio; on behalf of the Petitioners. JOHN Q. LEWIS, ESQ., Cleveland, Ohio; on behalf of Respondent Johnson. ALAN E. UNTEREINER, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent Dotson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Prisoners typically want two things: first, to improve their conditions while in prison; and second, to get out of prison as quickly as possible. Respondents' claims here are not conditions claims. They do not seek a larger cell or better food while in prison. Rather, their claims are about getting out of prison."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0000-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DOUGLAS R. COLE ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is this with an I or an E?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if they're successful on their claims, they're entitled to more frequent release hearings in the future."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They have to decide that again. That -- that order is void ab initio. It's as though it were never entered. They have to make a new decision about whether or not this person should -- should have parole and that they cannot in any way -- the State cannot rely on the prior decision that they reached on that issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought the only relief they were seeking was a more prompt next hearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But aren't -- aren't those claims moot or academic now? Because, as I understand it, he has had another parole hearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Was there -- maybe I'm wrong about this, but I thought there no challenge being made to the 2002 hearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why can't it simply be that prospectively for this class of prisoner, the old guidelines will apply, prospectively without undoing anything that's happened in the past?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Not exactly on the same plane, Your Honor, but recognizing that this Court in Balisok said that post-judgment administrative decisions regarding the duration of confinement also count as criminal judgments that are protected for purposes of -- of the Heck doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Your Honor, I believe what makes out the ex post facto claim is an increase in the quantum of punishment after they've committed their crimes. So they need to show that as an element."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do we have any case in which what was being -- what was sought to be challenged in a habeas action was not the duration of the sentence, but the procedure by which the duration of the sentence was determined?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And why would that be bad?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lewis (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEWIS: It's going to give States a license to violate civil rights that will otherwise not be protected under the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lewis (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEWIS: It's going to give States a license to violate civil rights that will otherwise not be protected under the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: You said -- you said a moment ago that it would be expanding habeas, and I'd like you to expand on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alan E. Untereiner (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ALAN E. UNTEREINER ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENT DOTSON"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: You want a 1983 hearing in which a United States district judge tells the parole commission, now, here are your marching orders for future cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-287",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e04bd805ece7f4ffb3b54fe027dcbeb5fb27b3a87fd93660ee3977593fb80fca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e04bd805ece7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Unless there are any further questions, we would ask that the Court affirm the Sixth Circuit's unanimous decision in favor of Dotson."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
